# Named function objects have proof-free denotation. Their closure theorem
# consumes the exact ordered parameter/domain evidence retained by Litex. The
# identity checks the proof-independent baseline.
have fn id(x R) R = x
id(1) = 1

# A compound body retains a verifier-owned WD DAG. Its In-C evidence is replayed
# locally inside `inc_closed`; `Litex.add` itself remains proof-free, and the
# checked definition is replayed at 1.
have fn inc(x R) R = x + 1
inc(1) = 1 + 1

# A partial body receives x != 0 from the same dependent requirements
# telescope and replays it locally beside the proof-free `Litex.div` term.
have fn reciprocal(x R: x != 0) R = 1 / x
forall a R:
    a != 0
    =>:
        reciprocal(a) = 1 / a

# Boundary: an unavailable defining-equality FactId cannot be reconstructed by
# target-side unfolding or proposition search; malformed body/domain WD edges
# are rejected before Lean emission.
